 "integration_notes": [
  "Replace the jaw meshes (collision + visual) by white_bodies/{l,r}_{fixed,moving}_white_body.stl: the original components minus the old inserts (fixed tip insert, moving inner insert) and minus the old 3 mm back plate (enclosed by the new strip). Keeping the original meshes would leave the old V-channel walls up to 6.6 mm above the fixed pad face and the old ridge 2.9 mm inside the fixed pad.",
  "Add every pad STL as its own collider on its link with physics:approximation convexHull (each piece is exactly convex, <= 40 vertices).",
  "Bind the pad physics material (static 1.2 / dynamic 0.9) to the pad colliders only. PhysX picks the higher-priority combine mode of a pair: with average on both, pad vs CRS plastic (0.4/0.3) gives 0.80/0.60; max gives 1.2/0.9; multiply gives 0.48/0.27.",
  "displayColor: pads beige, white bodies white (see colors).",
  "URDF link masses are explicit (0.271 / 0.093 kg). Pads add fixed +73.3 g, moving +41.1 g at 1.2 g/cm3; the removed old parts are 35.48 cm3 (fixed) and 28.37 cm3 (moving).",
  "Grasp G for the CRS top rim must move -2.83 mm along the ring normal (fixed pad otherwise 2.73 mm inside the ring)."
 ],
